      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let's denote the two numbers by \\( x \\) and \\( y \\). According to the problem, we have the following system of equations:\n\n1. \\( x + y = 6 \\)\n2. \\( x^2 - y^2 = 12 \\)\n\nWe can use the difference of squares formula to simplify the second equation. The difference of squares formula states that \\( x^2 - y^2 = (x + y)(x - y) \\). Substituting the value of \\( x + y \\) from the first equation into the second equation, we get:\n\n\\[ x^2 - y^2 = (x + y)(x - y) = 6(x - y) = 12 \\]\n\nTo find \\( x - y \\), we divide both sides of the equation by 6:\n\n\\[ x - y = \\frac{12}{6} = 2 \\]\n\nNow we have a system of two linear equations:\n\n1. \\( x + y = 6 \\)\n2. \\( x - y = 2 \\)\n\nWe can add these two equations together to eliminate \\( y \\):\n\n\\[ (x + y) + (x - y) = 6 + 2 \\]\n\\[ 2x = 8 \\]\n\\[ x = 4 \\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( x = 4 \\) back into the first equation to find \\( y \\):\n\n\\[ 4 + y = 6 \\]\n\\[ y = 6 - 4 \\]\n\\[ y = 2 \\]\n\nSo, the two numbers are \\( x = 4 \\) and \\( y = 2 \\). The positive difference between the two numbers is:\n\n\\[ |x - y| = |4 - 2| = 2 \\]\n\nTherefore, the positive difference of the two numbers is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
